  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 123 PM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nModel outputs and statistical aids have continued to suggest that \nheat will subtly rise to a peak on Saturday, concurrent with the \nstrengthening of ridging over the southwestern US and displacement \nof warm 850mb temperatures eastward. The coverage of triple-digit \nhighs is expected to be at their greatest extent Saturday with highs \nin the 100F to 103F range over the I-35 corridor and Rio Grande \nPlains. Without much deep-layer dryness to lower humidity, heat \nindices could approach Heat Advisory criteria across the I-35 \ncorridor, Coastal Plains, and Rio Grande Plains. Ambient \ntemperatures may decrease by a few degrees after Saturday as a humid \nsoutherly flow intensifies, but the added humidity may keep heat \nindices elevated into early next week. \n\nNext week, Z500 heights increase over the area as ridging \nstrengthens, but the focus of that ridging across ensembles is \ncentered over the southeastern US. This keeps a deep-layer \nsoutheasterly wind over our area, maintaining a humid airmass and \nflow off the Gulf. This will keep a low chance for occasional \nseabreeze showers over the Coastal Plains, but most of South-Central \nTexas will tend to stay dry. Expect high temperatures to stay in the \n90s to around 100F with lows remaining abnormally mild in the mid to \nupper 70s for most.",
